# Installed by xorgate at /etc/cron.d/xorgate-fake-hwclock (install.sh /
# `xorgate update`) — optimize-system-process-cycle plan, Phase 4.
#
# The stock Debian fake-hwclock saves the clock hourly (/etc/cron.hourly) +
# on clean shutdown; a hard crash (the undervoltage class this plan exists
# for) then restores a clock up to an hour stale on the next battery-less-RTC
# boot. Saving every 5 minutes bounds that restore error to <=5 min even with
# no GPS/LTE — which also keeps TLS cert validation and command-TTL logic
# sane at boot. The distro's hourly script is left untouched (a redundant
# save is harmless).
# Absolute path: cron.d entries run with PATH=/usr/bin:/bin, which does not
# include /sbin where fake-hwclock lives (hardware-verified 2026-07-29 — a
# `command -v` guard just fails silently under cron).
*/5 * * * * root [ -x /sbin/fake-hwclock ] && /sbin/fake-hwclock save
